  "notes": [
    "The 1/8 in tang: in the receiver the shank is held by bearing at the mouth and at its inner end \u2014 roughly 1,300 lbf at the mouth on a 2.5x bump, on a 1/8 in wall. Watch for dents and ovaling there; a 1/4 in wall (or a sleeve) for the 13 in shank adds ~2 lb.",
    "Under 3.5x on a bump, welded steel can crack at its welds over road miles before it would ever bend \u2014 the gusset plates take 82\u201390% of the moment off the riser's two corner welds."
